course: dictionary
lesson: 1832
title: Words with more than one job: coating
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. «The frying pan has a non-stick coating.» Here the coating is a thin layer that covers the pan.
explain: Try the swap check. «The cake had a coating of chocolate.» What covers the cake? A thin layer of chocolate. Put the word layer in the sentence: «The cake had a layer of chocolate.» It still makes sense, so coating means layer here.
explain: Coating can also be a verb, the -ing form of coat. «Snow was coating the hills» means the snow was covering the hills with a layer. The little word before it, was, is a clue that something is happening right now.
fact: A coating is a thin layer of something that covers a surface.
fact: Coating is the -ing form of coat, which means covering something with a layer.
fact: «A coating of dust» means a thin layer of dust on something.
fact: «A protective coating» keeps something safe, such as metal from rust.
fact: Clue words for coating are layer, cover, surface and thin.
exercise: «The non-stick coating on the frying pan stops food sticking.» What is the coating? | A lid that keeps heat in | A kind of food | *A thin layer that covers the pan | A metal handle for holding the pan
exercise: «Snow was coating the hills.» What is the snow doing? | Drawing a map of the hills | Melting the hills away | *Covering the hills with a layer | Counting the hills
exercise: «Sealants are thin plastic coatings painted into the grooves of back teeth.» What do sealants do? | Make the teeth bigger | Turn the teeth blue | Make the teeth glow in the dark | *Keep food and bacteria out
test: «A light coating of frost covered the car this morning.» What does coating mean here? | A bright colour | A long journey | A loud noise | *A thin layer
test: Dad is ___ the fish in breadcrumbs before he fries it. Which word fits the gap? | coat | cooked | *coating | cooling
exam: «The reflective coating on road signs makes them shine at night.» What does the reflective coating do? | Makes the sign heavy | Hides the sign from drivers | Turns the sign into a window | *Makes the sign shine at night
